WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.086 --> 00:00:03.326
(rush of wind)

00:00:03.326 --> 00:00:05.290
- Hello Believe Nation, my
name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:06.839
My one word is believe

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:08.949
and I believe that
entrepreneurs will solve

00:00:08.949 --> 00:00:11.325
all of the major problems in the world.

00:00:11.325 --> 00:00:13.130
I started the mentor
me series with the goal

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:16.276
to try to hang around people
who've done a lot more than us

00:00:16.276 --> 00:00:18.926
and hopefully by spending
more time with them

00:00:18.926 --> 00:00:20.424
some of their mindset, their thoughts,

00:00:20.424 --> 00:00:21.845
their beliefs, their attitudes,

00:00:21.845 --> 00:00:24.715
their way of looking at
at the world seeps into us

00:00:24.715 --> 00:00:27.769
to help up become the
best version of ourselves.

00:00:27.769 --> 00:00:30.182
So today we're going to
learn from Nelson Mandela

00:00:30.182 --> 00:00:31.844
and some of his best speeches.

00:00:31.844 --> 00:00:33.093
Mentor me, Nelson.

00:00:33.093 --> 00:00:35.013
Rule number three is my personal favorite

00:00:35.013 --> 00:00:37.370
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.897
And as always guys, as your watching

00:00:38.897 --> 00:00:41.137
if somebody says something
that really resonates with you

00:00:41.137 --> 00:00:42.920
please leave it down in the comments below

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:45.530
and put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:47.385
and when you write it down

00:00:47.385 --> 00:00:50.409
it's much more likely to
stick with yourself as well.

00:00:50.409 --> 00:00:51.242
Enjoy.

00:00:52.293 --> 00:00:56.126
(upbeat, inspirational music)

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:08.627
- I have fought very firmly
against white domination.

00:01:09.676 --> 00:01:13.843
I have fought very firmly
against black domination.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:18.741
I cherish the idea of a new South Africa

00:01:20.528 --> 00:01:23.536
where all South Africans are equal.

00:01:23.536 --> 00:01:26.703
For anybody who changes his principles

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:31.660
depending on whom he is dealing

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:34.288
that is not a man who can lead a nation.

00:01:34.288 --> 00:01:37.621
(enthusiastic applause)

00:02:02.702 --> 00:02:04.619
Apparently, Mr. Koppel,

00:02:07.514 --> 00:02:09.884
you have not listened to my argument.

00:02:09.884 --> 00:02:11.467
If you had done so,

00:02:13.012 --> 00:02:16.929
then you have not been
serious in examining it.

00:02:17.774 --> 00:02:21.191
I have replied to one of our friends here

00:02:22.596 --> 00:02:25.179
that I have refused to be drawn

00:02:26.534 --> 00:02:28.732
into the differences that exist

00:02:28.732 --> 00:02:33.255
between various communities
inside the U.S.A.

00:02:33.255 --> 00:02:37.422
You have not commented that
I'm going to offend anybody

00:02:38.527 --> 00:02:40.938
by refusing to involve myself

00:02:40.938 --> 00:02:43.641
in the internal affairs of the U.S.A.

00:02:43.641 --> 00:02:45.140
(clears throat)

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:47.390
(applause)

00:02:50.793 --> 00:02:55.372
Why are you so keen that
I should involve myself

00:02:55.372 --> 00:02:57.814
in the internal affairs of Cuba and Libya?

00:02:57.814 --> 00:02:58.647
- [Ted Koppel] No.

00:02:58.647 --> 00:03:01.147
I expect you to be consistent.

00:03:07.848 --> 00:03:09.654
I don't know if I've paralyzed you.

00:03:09.654 --> 00:03:10.874
- No, no, no, no--

00:03:10.874 --> 00:03:14.874
(raucous laughter and applause)

00:03:35.249 --> 00:03:36.082
Alright.

00:03:45.051 --> 00:03:45.884
I'm--

00:03:49.575 --> 00:03:50.847
I'm afraid, Mr. Mandela,

00:03:50.847 --> 00:03:53.602
that paralysis does not
set in quite that easily

00:03:53.602 --> 00:03:54.435
in my case.

00:03:54.435 --> 00:03:56.176
(laughter)

00:03:56.176 --> 00:03:57.338
The point--

00:03:57.338 --> 00:03:59.588
(applause)

00:04:02.798 --> 00:04:06.131
- When I phoned some place in my country

00:04:08.931 --> 00:04:11.764
and a lady answered the telephone,

00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:16.069
I then asked "To whom am I speaking?"

00:04:18.481 --> 00:04:20.206
She said, "you're speaking to me."

00:04:20.206 --> 00:04:23.122
(laughter)

00:04:23.122 --> 00:04:25.976
I said, "well, lady, I
know I'm speaking to you.

00:04:25.976 --> 00:04:26.809
(laughter)

00:04:26.809 --> 00:04:29.048
But what's your name?"

00:04:29.048 --> 00:04:30.801
She said, "Who are you to ask for my name?

00:04:30.801 --> 00:04:31.750
What's your name?"

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.000
(laughter)

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:38.440
I said, "Well, lady, as soon
as you tell me your name,

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:40.107
I'll tell you mine."

00:04:41.071 --> 00:04:45.238
But as we argued as to who
should tell his or her name

00:04:46.106 --> 00:04:47.939
she became very cross.

00:04:48.903 --> 00:04:53.164
And she said, "you seem
to be a vapid person.

00:04:53.164 --> 00:04:56.062
Have you passed your matric?"

00:04:56.062 --> 00:05:00.229
Now matric in our country is a
university entry examination.

00:05:02.307 --> 00:05:05.936
And I said, "well, lady,
you must be very careful.

00:05:05.936 --> 00:05:08.784
Because if the qualification
to speak to you

00:05:08.784 --> 00:05:12.142
is the possession of a matric certificate

00:05:12.142 --> 00:05:15.948
I might work hard and pass my matric

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:19.031
and be in the same class as you are."

00:05:19.979 --> 00:05:21.396
That was treason.

00:05:23.106 --> 00:05:26.606
She said, "you will never be in my class."

00:05:27.885 --> 00:05:29.404
And banged the telephone.

00:05:29.404 --> 00:05:32.259
(laughter)

00:05:32.259 --> 00:05:34.856
How I wish she were here today.

00:05:34.856 --> 00:05:39.023
(laughter and enthusiastic applause)

00:05:51.803 --> 00:05:55.803
She would now discover
that I have achieved more

00:05:56.728 --> 00:05:58.395
than pass my matric.

00:05:59.809 --> 00:06:01.976
The very right to be human

00:06:03.376 --> 00:06:04.959
is denied every day

00:06:05.956 --> 00:06:08.901
to hundreds of millions of people

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:11.451
as a result of poverty

00:06:11.451 --> 00:06:15.384
and the unavailability
of basic necessities

00:06:15.384 --> 00:06:18.551
such as food, jobs, water and shelter,

00:06:20.933 --> 00:06:25.100
education, health care,
and a healthy environment.

00:06:28.217 --> 00:06:30.634
As I sit in Qunu, my village,

00:06:32.996 --> 00:06:35.829
and grow as ancient as it's hills,

00:06:38.206 --> 00:06:41.289
I will continue to entertain the hope

00:06:42.704 --> 00:06:46.669
that there has emerged a cadre of leaders

00:06:46.669 --> 00:06:49.015
in my own country and region,

00:06:49.015 --> 00:06:51.034
on my continent,

00:06:51.034 --> 00:06:52.862
and in the world,

00:06:52.862 --> 00:06:57.048
which will not allow that any
should be denied their freedom

00:06:57.048 --> 00:06:57.965
as we were;

00:06:59.741 --> 00:07:03.466
that any should be turned into refugees

00:07:03.466 --> 00:07:04.383
as we were;

00:07:05.279 --> 00:07:08.726
that any should be condemned to go hungry

00:07:08.726 --> 00:07:09.643
as we were;

00:07:10.991 --> 00:07:14.583
that any should be stripped
of their human dignity

00:07:14.583 --> 00:07:15.500
as we were.

00:08:43.436 --> 00:08:46.519
- When you were convicted in 1964 for

00:08:49.713 --> 00:08:52.113
conspiracy against the state.

00:08:52.113 --> 00:08:53.078
And in your,

00:08:53.078 --> 00:08:54.655
when you pleaded you said that,

00:08:54.655 --> 00:08:57.738
"I am willing to die for this cause."

00:08:59.024 --> 00:09:01.543
This is a very tough thing to say.

00:09:01.543 --> 00:09:02.376
- Yes.

00:09:04.118 --> 00:09:05.695
I had to say that.

00:09:05.695 --> 00:09:08.617
Not from a spirit of bravado,

00:09:08.617 --> 00:09:10.578
but because I genuinely felt

00:09:10.578 --> 00:09:13.369
that they were going to hang us.

00:09:13.369 --> 00:09:17.202
And it is the desire of
every freedom fighter,

00:09:18.106 --> 00:09:21.532
to disappear under a cloud of glory

00:09:21.532 --> 00:09:23.615
rather than that of fame.

00:09:24.513 --> 00:09:27.363
It is the task of a freedom fighter,

00:09:27.363 --> 00:09:31.822
when you see that the end
of your days has come,

00:09:31.822 --> 00:09:35.739
to leave a tradition of
bravery, determination,

00:09:37.437 --> 00:09:40.270
to face death for your principles.

00:09:41.785 --> 00:09:43.702
And I thought about it.

00:09:45.114 --> 00:09:47.759
It was not because I was brave.

00:09:47.759 --> 00:09:51.926
But because one had a duty
to perform at that moment.

00:09:53.145 --> 00:09:55.145
I have dedicated my life

00:09:58.042 --> 00:09:59.375
to this struggle

00:10:01.289 --> 00:10:03.122
of the African people.

00:10:05.866 --> 00:10:09.116
I have fought against white domination.

00:10:14.309 --> 00:10:17.892
And I have fought
against black domination.

00:10:21.084 --> 00:10:23.251
I have cherished the ideal

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:28.361
of a democratic

00:10:28.361 --> 00:10:29.694
and free society

00:10:31.336 --> 00:10:35.503
in which all persons will
live together in harmony

00:10:37.343 --> 00:10:39.760
and with equal opportunities.

00:10:47.388 --> 00:10:50.971
It is an ideal for
which I hope to live for

00:10:56.236 --> 00:10:57.903
and to see realized.

00:11:01.479 --> 00:11:03.729
But my Lord, if it need be,

00:11:07.866 --> 00:11:09.033
it is an ideal

00:11:10.511 --> 00:11:13.094
for which I am prepared to die.

00:11:14.508 --> 00:11:17.675
In 1993 I was walking along the street

00:11:22.742 --> 00:11:25.325
when I met a couple of tourists

00:11:26.658 --> 00:11:29.491
from a well known Western country.

00:11:31.753 --> 00:11:35.495
And then the husband stopped and said,

00:11:35.495 --> 00:11:36.662
"Mr. Mandela."

00:11:38.795 --> 00:11:41.909
I said, "Many people
mistake me for that chap."

00:11:41.909 --> 00:11:44.159
(laughter)

00:11:46.011 --> 00:11:48.469
And he said, "Would I be entitled also

00:11:48.469 --> 00:11:51.473
to mistake you for that chap?"

00:11:51.473 --> 00:11:55.640
I say, "Well you'll be
doing what many people do."

00:11:56.653 --> 00:11:58.806
He then turned to his wife and said,

00:11:58.806 --> 00:12:00.723
"Darling, Mr. Mandela."

00:12:03.462 --> 00:12:05.712
She was completely unimpressed.

00:12:05.712 --> 00:12:07.600
(laughter)

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:10.105
And she said, "What is he famous for?"

00:12:10.105 --> 00:12:12.355
(laughter)

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:18.446
And the husband, in his
embarrassment dropped the voice

00:12:18.446 --> 00:12:21.167
and he said, "Mr. Mandela, Mr. Mandela."

00:12:21.167 --> 00:12:23.504
(laughter)

00:12:23.504 --> 00:12:25.837
And that the dear lady said,

00:12:28.017 --> 00:12:30.376
"But I asked you what is he famous for?"

00:12:30.376 --> 00:12:32.385
(laughter)

00:12:32.385 --> 00:12:35.958
And without waiting for an
answer from the husband,

00:12:35.958 --> 00:12:38.092
she turned to me and said,

00:12:38.092 --> 00:12:39.453
"What are you famous for?"

00:12:39.453 --> 00:12:40.976
(laughter)

00:12:40.976 --> 00:12:43.538
I must confess, I couldn't
answer that question.

00:12:43.538 --> 00:12:44.840
(laugher)

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:47.810
We are therefore pleased to announce

00:12:47.810 --> 00:12:50.323
that we're able once again

00:12:50.323 --> 00:12:52.987
to increase old age benefits.

00:12:52.987 --> 00:12:56.320
(enthusiastic applause)

00:12:58.853 --> 00:13:01.005
I'm very excited about this.

00:13:01.005 --> 00:13:04.338
(laughter and applause)

00:13:11.476 --> 00:13:14.059
Because in Davos in Switzerland

00:13:16.015 --> 00:13:18.182
I told the plenary session

00:13:20.677 --> 00:13:24.844
that in a few months, I'll
be standing next to the road,

00:13:27.369 --> 00:13:29.119
saying, "Please help.

00:13:30.143 --> 00:13:31.060
Unemployed.

00:13:34.108 --> 00:13:34.941
No money.

00:13:37.019 --> 00:13:38.201
A new wife."

00:13:38.201 --> 00:13:41.118
(raucous laughter)

00:13:42.094 --> 00:13:43.520
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:45.597
I'd love to know what did
you think of this video?

00:13:45.597 --> 00:13:47.590
What was your favorite clip and why?

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:50.374
What lesson are you going
to pull from this clip

00:13:50.374 --> 00:13:52.328
and immediately apply somehow

00:13:52.328 --> 00:13:54.461
to your life or to your business?

00:13:54.461 --> 00:13:56.009
Please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:13:56.009 --> 00:13:57.283
I'm super curious to find out.

00:13:57.283 --> 00:13:58.586
I also want to give a quick shout out

00:13:58.586 --> 00:14:01.394
to Anthony Avina from Anthony Avina Vlogs.

00:14:01.394 --> 00:14:04.136
Anthony, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book

00:14:04.136 --> 00:14:05.111
Your One Word

00:14:05.111 --> 00:14:07.015
and doing that vlog review on it.

00:14:07.015 --> 00:14:08.586
I really appreciate the support, man,

00:14:08.586 --> 00:14:10.401
and I'm glad you enjoyed the read.

00:14:10.401 --> 00:14:12.798
- Today I'm going to be
reviewing a book for you guys

00:14:12.798 --> 00:14:16.069
called Your One Word by Evan Carmichael.

00:14:16.069 --> 00:14:17.483
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:14:17.483 --> 00:14:18.858
I believe in you,

00:14:18.858 --> 00:14:20.838
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:14:20.838 --> 00:14:23.318
and whatever your one word is.

00:14:23.318 --> 00:14:25.680
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:28.144
(rush of wind)

